api_sketch:
Handshake (WS/SSE): client -> {client_id, api_key, desired_frame_types:[progress,patch,action,commit], window_size, preferred_latency_ms, allowed_tools:[tool_a,tool_b], resume_token:? }
Server -> {durable_session_id, initial_model, first_frame_seq}
Example frames as standalone JSON envelopes (newline-delimited):
{"seq":1, "type":"progress", "stable_prefix":"Summarized:", "delta":" ... partial text ...", "legibility_score":0.42}
{"seq":2, "type":"action", "action_id":"act-23", "tool_id":"search-index", "payload":{"query":"error logs 23"}, "idempotency":"uuid-1234"}
{"seq":2.1, "type":"action_ack", "action_id":"act-23", "status":"accepted", "trace_link":"https://console.redwood.ai/trace/abc"}
{"seq":3, "type":"patch", "ops":[{"op":"replace-range","start":12,"end":16,"text":"refined"}], "derived_from":2}
{"seq":4, "type":"commit", "final_schema":"{\"title\":\"string\",\"steps\":\"array\"}" }
Notes: frames must be small (<=32KB) where possible; clients should be able to process frames incrementally. Handshake must be authenticated and indicate whether tool calling is allowed.
